      "title": "Partial disability",
      "narration": "Rosa recovers enough to work half days but cannot do the heavy parts of her trade. A partial disability benefit pays a flat percentage of the total disability benefit, commonly 50 percent, for a limited time, often six months. Traditional partial disability benefits require that the insured first was totally disabled and then returned to work part time or in a reduced capacity. If Rosa’s total benefit is 3,600 dollars, her partial benefit is 1,800 dollars a month for up to six months. The flat percentage is simple but ignores how much income she actually lost.",
