      "narration": "A residual disability benefit replaces the lost share of income instead of a flat percentage. The formula is the percentage of income lost, multiplied by the total disability benefit. Rosa earned 6,000 dollars; working half days she earns 3,600, a 40 percent loss. Her residual benefit is 40 percent of 3,600, which is 1,440 dollars a month, for as long as the income loss continues within the benefit period. Most residual provisions require at least a 20 percent income loss to pay and treat a loss of 75 or 80 percent as total. Residual benefits do not require a prior period of total disability.",
